&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Manager, Compliance within CX Global Financial Crimes Operations (GFCO), you&#39;ll join the Functional Lead team, a high-performing group responsible for ensuring Coinbase&#39;s compliance operations programs across Transaction Monitoring (TM), Screening, and Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) operate effectively and efficiently. You&#39;ll own the compliance content function across all three pillars, lead a small team of contractors, and serve as an operational program manager for the TM function. You&#39;ll drive measurable efficiency gains by embedding AI into compliance content operations while maintaining rigorous quality standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end content lifecycle across TM, Screening, and EDD, managing intake, prioritization, creation, review, approval, publishing, and change communication for all procedural content, guidance documents, and job aids&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a small team of 2-3 contractors, assigning work, setting priorities, and ensuring consistent quality and delivery against deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive program management for the TM function, hosting weekly change management meetings, tracking the book of work, resolving blockers, and reporting progress to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deploy AI agents and automated workflows to scale content production, streamline intake processes, and reduce manual effort across daily operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Engineering, L&amp;amp;D, Operations, 2nd Line Compliance, and Program teams to align content and process changes across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the AI strategy for the content domain, identifying opportunities for automation, building agent-driven solutions, and driving adoption across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in compliance operations, financial crimes, AML/BSA, or related regulatory environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated program management track record, including managing 3+ cross-functional initiatives simultaneously with structured tracking and deadline-driven delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience applying AML/BSA, transaction monitoring, sanctions screening, or EDD regulatory frameworks in an operational context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and manage AI agents and automated workflows, including driving AI strategy and adoption within a functional domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing content lifecycles or knowledge management functions in a regulated environment, with published outputs used by front-line operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
