&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Payroll Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;on the Global Payroll team, you&#39;ll lead biweekly payroll processing for all U.S. salaried and hourly employees. The Global Payroll team manages end-to-end payroll operations across five continents, partnering with HR, Finance, Accounting, and Legal to deliver accurate, compliant, and scalable payroll services. You&#39;ll own the full U.S. payroll cycle, including equity-related payroll, and serve as the go-to resource for resolving employee payroll inquiries with speed and precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end biweekly U.S. payroll processing for salaried and hourly employees, including daily payroll cycles for non-qualified stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute payroll input compilation from multiple sources, validating data for accuracy and completeness before each cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive timely resolution of employee payroll inquiries in Jira within SLA, performing root cause analysis to prevent recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR, Finance, and cross-functional teams to process employee changes in payroll and cross-check data accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead timecard tracking and reconciliation to ensure alignment between timekeeping systems and payroll records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous process improvements by identifying opportunities for automation and efficiency gains in payroll workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-state payroll processing experience, with demonstrated expertise in federal, state, and local tax compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience processing payroll for employee populations that receive equity compensation, including restricted stock units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on proficiency with payroll platforms (e.g., UKG Pro, Workday HCM) and HRIS integrations in a high-volume environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of resolving complex payroll issues independently, with documented root cause analysis and process improvement outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Workspace, Slack, Atlassian tools (Jira), and Apple products for daily collaboration and case management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with cloud-native data environments (e.g., Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery) and their metadata, lineage, and governance capabilities at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
