&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Protective Intelligence team within Security helps protect Coinbase&#39;s people, assets, and reputation through intelligence, due diligence, and geopolitical risk analysis. As the team scales alongside Coinbase&#39;s global growth, this &lt;strong&gt;Strategic Intelligence Manager &lt;/strong&gt;role serves as the individual-contributor expert and directly responsible individual (DRI) for the Strategic Intelligence program. You&#39;ll set the strategic direction for the program, lead high-impact due diligence for M&amp;amp;A and executive-level decisions, and deliver forward-looking geopolitical assessments that shape how Coinbase operates and grows around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategic direction and governance of Coinbase&#39;s Strategic Intelligence program, serving as the recognized subject-matter expert across reputational due diligence, geopolitical intelligence, and first-party diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Reputational Due Diligence for mergers and acquisitions, investments, and strategic partnerships, producing complex risk findings that inform Corporate Development and executive decision-making within defined SLAs and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver forward-looking geopolitical intelligence, assessing how events and crises impact Coinbase offices, personnel, assets, and business strategy, and routing timely assessments to senior leadership, GSOC, Executive Protection, and Business Continuity teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source and establish open and closed-source intelligence streams while building deep relationships with public and private-sector intelligence partners to proactively identify threats targeting Coinbase and the crypto community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable, AI-enabled processes that increase program efficiency and reduce cost while maintaining appropriate human-in-the-loop safeguards, and define program metrics that communicate impact to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor analysts, specialists, and contractors, including senior teammates, providing high-signal feedback on judgment, influence, and craft and elevating standards across complex, ambiguous work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in intelligence, due diligence, geopolitical risk analysis, investigations, or related fields, with recognized expertise in at least one intelligence domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record producing investigation and geopolitical risk reports that have directly informed M&amp;amp;A, investment, or other business decisions at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead initiatives independently from problem identification through solution delivery, owning a defined capability within a broader program while holding cross-functional partners and vendors accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates complex technical and business risks clearly to senior audiences in written and verbal formats, ensuring stakeholders are rarely surprised by outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applies systems thinking to anticipate second-order impacts and designs for long-term resilience and scale across intelligence operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
